{"name":"Astral Aura","hex":"#363151","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"astral","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to or resembling the stars; starry.","Relating to an aster."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A supernatural being from the astral plane."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/astral"},{"term":"aura","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A subtle emanation or exhalation of any substance, such as an aroma or odour. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A distinctive atmosphere or quality surrounding or associated with something or someone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aura"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aura (paranormal)","blocks":[{"text":"In parapsychology and some spiritual traditions, an aura, or energy field, is said to be an emanation produced by and surrounding the body of a person, animal or object, unique to the individual, and which is typically regarded to be an ever present and essential part of its being. In some esoteric positions, the aura is described as a subtle body. Psychics and holistic medicine practitioners often claim to have the ability to see the size, color and type of vibration of an aura."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Aura_diagram.png/330px-Aura_diagram.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aura_(paranormal)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg/250px-Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/51/Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg/250px-Charles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Charles Webster Leadbeater is credited with developing and popularizing the concept of auras.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharles_Webster_Leadbeater.019.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Lotus_Kirlian.jpg/330px-Lotus_Kirlian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Lotus_Kirlian.jpg/330px-Lotus_Kirlian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An artistic representation of a man in the Lotus position, surrounded by a blue glow","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALotus_Kirlian.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Baraducforcevital.tif/lossless-page1-250px-Baraducforcevital.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Baraducforcevital.tif/lossless-page1-250px-Baraducforcevital.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Picture by Hippolyte Baraduc published in 1896, purported to show a \"vital force\" around a child","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaraducforcevital.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Aura_testing.jpg/250px-Aura_testing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/64/Aura_testing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Aura_testing.jpg/250px-Aura_testing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An aura reader tested in a controlled experiment at the Observatoire Zététique, May 2004","link":"https:/